# K03 S6 control (Codex K03-CALLABLE-PATH-20261007-25): handed to a callable formal, a path that selects a callable is the
# occurrence it selects -- a reference the formal receives, not a call: apply calls it once, after reading the count,
# which is still 0 then.  Holder runs nothing (`bump()` would count).  v is 1 * 10 + 0: exit 7; 81 Holder ran, 83 a wrong
# value (the path called before apply).
int: hits 0
int: seen 0
fn: tick () int
    node\hits: node\hits + 1
    return: node\hits
end: tick
fn: bump () int
    node\seen: node\seen + 1
    return: 0
end: bump
fn: count () int
    return: node\hits
end: count
fn: saw () int
    return: node\seen
end: saw
Holder:
    fn: tick
    bump()
end: Holder
fn: apply (tick: f) int
    int: before count()
    int: r f()
    return: r * 10 + before
end: apply
fn: run () int
    int: v apply(Holder\tick)
    if: saw() != 0
        return: 81
    if: v != 10
        return: 83
    return: 7
end: run
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: run(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
